<title>USA: American Airlines details passenger plans.</title>
<headline>American Airlines details passenger plans.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMR Corp's American Airlines said Thursday that if its pilots strike, passengers of canceled flights could reschedule at a later date without penalty or service charge.</p>
<p>The company said it continued to &quot;work diligently&quot; to reach a settlement with the Allied Pilots Asociation, the union that represents American's pilots, or persuade the union to accept binding arbitation.</p>
<p>In addition to waving the charge for postponed flights, the company said if travel plans cannot be deferred, passengers can request refunds on tickets, if they have not been used on another airline.</p>
<p>American also said it will attempt to book passengers on another airline if seats are available.</p>
</text>
